WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
Reflective notes make learning reusable.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:16.808
Personal learning journals, decision records, practice logs, incident notes, and project retrospectives all serve the same broad purpose: they capture context before memory turns the event into a simplified story.

3
00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:24.218
The best notes are useful because they are specific enough to review and lightweight enough to actually keep using.

4
00:00:24.218 --> 00:00:30.101
A useful note captures context, assumptions, choices, tradeoffs, outcomes, and lessons.

5
00:00:30.101 --> 00:00:41.408
For a decision record, that might include the options considered, the evidence available, the constraints, the chosen path, and what would cause the decision to be revisited.

6
00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:50.041
For a practice log, it might include what was attempted, what feedback appeared, what improved, and what needs focused practice next.

7
00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:52.944
Notes should be searchable and easy to apply.

8
00:00:52.944 --> 00:01:00.584
Long essays can be valuable, but many teams and individuals sustain reflection better with short structured prompts.

9
00:01:00.584 --> 00:01:09.828
A recurring format such as context, decision, evidence, result, lesson, and next action can make notes easier to write and easier to scan later.

10
00:01:09.828 --> 00:01:13.954
The format should support learning, not become the work itself.

11
00:01:13.954 --> 00:01:19.989
The strongest reflective notes become patterns, checklists, examples, and future prompts.

12
00:01:19.989 --> 00:01:23.504
A debugging lesson may become a diagnostic checklist.

13
00:01:23.504 --> 00:01:26.636
A project lesson may become a planning question.

14
00:01:26.636 --> 00:01:29.692
An incident lesson may become a runbook update.

15
00:01:29.692 --> 00:01:33.206
A communication lesson may become a pre-brief prompt.

16
00:01:33.206 --> 00:01:39.547
Reflection becomes more valuable when it changes the tools and routines people will use next time.
